{"name":"Basmati White","hex":"#ebe1c9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"basmati","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A variety of long-grain rice, notable for its fragrance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basmati"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Basmati","blocks":[{"text":"Basmati is a variety of long, slender-grained aromatic rice which originates from the Indian subcontinent, mainly in the regions of Haryana, Punjab, Sindh and many other states and provinces of India, Pakistan and Nepal. As of 2019, India accounted for 65% of the international trade in basmati rice, while Pakistan accounted for the remaining 35%. Many countries use domestically grown basmati rice crops; however, basmati is geographically exclusive to certain districts of India and Pakistan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Khyma_and_Basmati_rice.jpg/330px-Khyma_and_Basmati_rice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basmati","wikidata":"Q1649635"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Cooked_cilantro_lime_dish_basmati_rice_India.jpg/500px-Cooked_cilantro_lime_dish_basmati_rice_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Cooked_cilantro_lime_dish_basmati_rice_India.jpg/1280px-Cooked_cilantro_lime_dish_basmati_rice_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Cooked_cilantro_lime_dish_basmati_rice_India.jpg/500px-Cooked_cilantro_lime_dish_basmati_rice_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"White basmati rice cooked with Burmese fish mint","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACooked_cilantro_lime_dish_basmati_rice_India.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Rice_in_Electric_Cooker.jpg/500px-Rice_in_Electric_Cooker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Rice_in_Electric_Cooker.jpg/1280px-Rice_in_Electric_Cooker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Rice_in_Electric_Cooker.jpg/500px-Rice_in_Electric_Cooker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Long Grain Basmati rice is widely used for many meat and vegetarian curries in India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARice_in_Electric_Cooker.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/